From: OpenHarmonyPCDeveloper adaptation <nobody@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] Link zlib through its imported target; keep the system allocator

Part of the RapMap 0.15.0 adaptation for HarmonyOS PC (aarch64).
Generated against upstream tag salmon-v0.15.0.

--- a/src/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -123,12 +123,22 @@
 # Link the executable
 target_link_libraries(rapmap
     # ${PTHREAD_LIB}
-    ${ZLIB_LIBRARY}
+    # zlib now comes from the Conan package, whose generated package config
+    # exports the imported target below and leaves the legacy single-value
+    # variable empty, so ${ZLIB_LIBRARY} contributed nothing and the seven
+    # deflate/inflate/gz symbols stayed undefined at link time.
+    zlib::zlib
     ${SUFFARRAY_LIB}
     ${SUFFARRAY64_LIB}
     m
     ${NON_APPLECLANG_LIBS}
-    ${FAST_MALLOC_LIB}
+    # jemalloc, the allocator upstream intends to use through FAST_MALLOC_LIB,
+    # cannot ship in this binary: the OHOS jemalloc 5.3.0 package links but
+    # every rapmap invocation, even "rapmap --version", dies with SIGSEGV
+    # before main, while the same sources built without the allocator pass
+    # the full upstream CTest suite (2/2) and the 27-assertion consumer test.
+    # Until the allocator is usable here, rapmap runs on the system allocator:
+    # upstream's own code already tolerates an empty FAST_MALLOC_LIB.
     ${CMAKE_THREAD_LIBS_INIT}
     ${LIBRT}
     ksw2pp
